  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p>Thanks to the collective enthusiasm for sharing NutritionFacts.org by our <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\">subscribers</a>, <a href=\"https://twitter.com/nutrition_facts\">Twitter</a> and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/nutrition_facts_org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Instagram</a> followers, and 1.5 million <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org\">Facebook</a> and <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/+NutritionfactsOrgMD\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">G+</a> fans, we averaged millions of video views a month this year. But it’s not about the numbers; it’s about the people whose lives we’ve touched, changed, or even saved. That is why I’ve dedicated my life to get new videos and articles up each and every day. A heartfelt thank you to <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donors/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">everyone</a> who has made this public service possible.</p>\n<p>NutritionFacts.org arises from my annual review of the medical literature. With the help of a team of hundreds of volunteers, we churned through tens of thousands of papers published in the peer-reviewed scientific nutrition literature and are ramping up to break new records in 2018. How do I choose which studies to highlight? In general, I strive to focus on the most groundbreaking, interesting, and useful findings; but which topics resonate the most? Is it the practical ones, offering cooking or shopping tips? Or those that dissect the studies behind the headlines? Maybe it’s the geeky science ones exploring the wonderfully weird world of human biology? As you can see from the below list, the answer seems to be a bit of all of the above:</p>\n<h3><strong>#10 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-avocados-healthy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Are Avocados Healthy?</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-avocados-healthy/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51678\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-10-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>Actually, all the avocado videos were really popular this year. Also check out <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/effects-of-avocados-and-red-wine-on-meal-induced-inflammation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Effects of Avocados and Red Wine on Meal-Induced Inflammation</a>, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-avocados-good-for-your-cholesterol/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Are Avocados Good for Your Cholesterol?</a>, and <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/Avocados-Lower-Small-Dense-LDL-Cholesterol/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Avocados Lower Small Dense LDL Cholesterol</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#9 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/what-does-a-low-white-blood-cell-count-mean/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">What Does a Low White Blood Cell Count Mean?</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/what-does-a-low-white-blood-cell-count-mean/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51676\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-09-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>I figured this would be popular since it was a popular question I get, followed by <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/What-Is-the-Ideal-White-Blood-Cell-Count/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">What Is the Ideal White Blood Cell Count?</a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#8 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-food-to-counter-the-effects-of-air-pollution/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Best Foods to Counter the Effects of Air Pollution</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-food-to-counter-the-effects-of-air-pollution/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51674\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-08-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>The picture kind of gives it away :). This was one of many popular Best Food for X videos this year, including <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-foods-to-reduce-stroke-risk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Best Foods to Reduce Stroke Risk</a>, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-supplements-for-prostate-cancer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Best Supplements for Prostate Cancer</a>, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-best-food-for-high-cholesterol/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Best Food for High Cholesterol</a>, <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-foods-for-polycystic-ovary-syndrome-pcos/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Best Foods for Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS)</a>, and <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/best-foods-to-improve-sexual-function/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Best Foods to Improve Sexual Function</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#7 <a title=\"Ginger for Migraines\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gundrys-the-plant-paradox-is-wrong/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"bookmark noopener noreferrer\">Dr. Gundry’s The Plant Paradox is Wrong</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gundrys-the-plant-paradox-is-wrong/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51672\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-07-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>This was such a popular video it tempts me to do more analyses of the popular press. Let me know if any new books come out you’d like me to look at.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#6 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-our-gut-bacteria-can-use-eggs-to-accelerate-cancer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Our Gut Bacteria Can Use Eggs to Accelerate Cancer</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-our-gut-bacteria-can-use-eggs-to-accelerate-cancer/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51670\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-06-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>The other two really popular microbiome videos this year were <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-develop-a-healthy-gut-ecosystem/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How to Develop a Healthy Gut Ecosystem</a> and <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/microbiome-we-are-what-they-eat/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microbiome: We Are What They Eat</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#5 <a title=\"What Causes Diabetes?\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/what-about-coconuts-coconut-milk-and-coconut-oil-mcts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"bookmark noopener noreferrer\">What about Coconuts, Coconut Milk, &amp; Coconut Oil MCTs?</a> </strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/what-about-coconuts-coconut-milk-and-coconut-oil-mcts/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51668\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-05-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>The other coconut oil one I did was also really popular:<a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/coconut-oil-and-the-boost-in-hdl-good-cholesterol/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> Coconut Oil &amp; the Boost in HDL “Good” Cholesterol</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#4 <a title=\"The Okinawa Diet: Living to 100\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-prevent-blood-sugar-and-triglyceride-spikes-after-meals/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"bookmark noopener noreferrer\">How to Prevent Blood Sugar and Triglyceride Spikes After Meals</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-prevent-blood-sugar-and-triglyceride-spikes-after-meals/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51666\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-04-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>Within hours of eating an unhealthy meal, we can get a spike in inflammation, crippling our artery function, thickening our blood, and causing a fight-or-flight nerve response. But there are foods we can eat at every meal to counter this reaction.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#3 <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-greger-in-the-kitchen-my-new-favorite-beverage/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dr. Greger in the Kitchen: My New Favorite Beverage</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-greger-in-the-kitchen-my-new-favorite-beverage/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51664\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-03-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>I had a feeling people would like this! I also did <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-greger-in-the-kitchen-my-new-favorite-dessert/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Greger in the Kitchen: My New Favorite Dessert</a> and I’m toying with a New Favorite Breakfast, but first I want to get it just right!</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#2 <a title=\"The Problem With the Paleo Diet Argument\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/which-are-better-chia-seeds-or-flax-seeds/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"bookmark noopener noreferrer\">Which Are Better: Chia Seeds or Flax Seeds?</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/which-are-better-chia-seeds-or-flax-seeds/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51662\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"114\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-02-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a>I think this was so popular because of all the traffic we got from Google of people asking this exact queston. Well, what effect do chia seeds have on weight loss, blood sugar, cholesterol, blood pressure, and inflammation? Click the video to find out!</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3><strong>#1 <a title=\"Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet\" href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"bookmark noopener noreferrer\">Dr. Greger’s Daily Dozen Checklist</a></strong></h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-51660\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01.png 8084w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-960x544.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-768x435.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-1024x581.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-1200x680.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-720x408.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-540x306.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-353x200.png 353w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/01/Top-10-01-921x522.png 921w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>In my book <a href=\"https://NutritionFacts.org/book/\">How Not to Die</a>, I center my recommendations around a Daily Dozen checklist of all the things I try to fit into my daily routine. This video version was so popular, that on January 26th we’ll be posting a second version up on the site to see which design people like better.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Yours in evidence-based nutrition—and… a happy, healthy new year!</p>\n<p>In health,</p>\n<p><b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"http://www.nutritionfacts.us5.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913&amp;id=40f9e497d1\"><u><b>here</b></u></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><u><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><u><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><u><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><u><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><u><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></u></a></li>\n</ul>"
  }
}
